<h2>How to stop autoplay</h2>

<h3>Firefox</h3>
<p>Settings &gt; Privacy &amp; Security &gt; Permissions &gt; Autoplay &gt; Settings&hellip;<br>
Set "Default for all websites" to <b>Block Audio and Video</b>, then click Save Changes.<br>
(Firefox already blocks autoplay with sound by default. This also blocks muted video.)</p>

<h3>Edge</h3>
<p>Settings &gt; Cookies and site permissions &gt; Media autoplay<br>
(or open <code>edge://settings/content/mediaAutoplay</code>)<br>
Set it to <b>Block</b>. "Limit" is gentler and is the default.</p>

<h3>Brave</h3>
<p>Open <code>brave://settings/content/autoplay</code><br>
(or Settings &gt; Privacy and security &gt; Site and Shields Settings &gt; Autoplay)<br>
Set it to <b>Block</b>.</p>

<h3>Vivaldi</h3>
<p>Settings &gt; Privacy and Security &gt; Default Permissions<br>
Set Autoplay to <b>Block</b>. On newer versions it may be under Settings &gt; Webpages &gt; Site Settings.</p>

<p><i>Note: Brave, Edge and Vivaldi are all built on Chromium, and none of them can stop every video and some sites will get around the setting. If a site still autoplays, an extension that disables HTML5 autoplay may help (although I havent faced any issues).</i></p>

